Z||000000||Kasdan||08-13-2001||08:01 PM||||Occasionally, when i start up my 86 GT, something starts squealing REALLY LOUD.  sometimes not at all, sometimes for a matter of seconds, sometimes for a minuite or more.  Keep in mind, that the a/c belt is off, the alternator belt is new, and the 3rd belt for my custom power steeting unit is new also.  Also, the water pump is brand new.||||reg||4
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-13-2001||08:30 PM||||Even though those belts are new they could be loose and slip and squeel.It couldnt hurt to retighten them ,maybe they streched||||reg||1
Z||000002||terryk||08-13-2001||08:52 PM||||Alternator, especially if the upper bolt threads in the bracket are stripped. It won't stay tight.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Kasdan||08-13-2001||09:26 PM||||oh god...2.8 alternaters are a ***** ...||||reg||1
Z||000004||2birds||08-13-2001||10:33 PM||||Make sure you aren't losing oil from the front crank seal or antifreeze from the water pump weep hole(imminent bearing failure).  My 2.8 squeal has been caused by both.  You can get a sleeve kit to fix the front crank seal problem for less than $10.  The seal wears a groove in the balancer, and eventually starts to leak there, especially if the seal has been replaced recently.||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroSoul||08-14-2001||06:53 AM||||  What does your voltmeter say during the squeal. An alternator stuck at full output will sometimes squeal on start up.||||reg||3
Z||000006||Wolfhound||08-14-2001||07:41 AM||||Take a close look at the pully surfaces and check for glazing. It may tell you which belt is slipping.<P>Would you like to go into more detail about the custom power steering?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000007||Kasdan||08-14-2001||09:17 AM||||I dont know very much detail about the power steering.  I do know that it was added to the car shortly after it was purchased.  There is a billit bracket connected to the top 2 bolts of the water pump (longer screws) and the power steering pump has its own pully.  It works GREAT.  I do think i need my front end sligned though, it drifts ever so slightly to the left.||||reg||1
